# C4 Level 1 — System Context: Industrial telemetry platform (illustrative reference architecture)
direction: right

classes: {
  person: {shape: c4-person}
  system: {style.border-radius: 8; style.stroke-width: 2}
  external: {style.stroke-dash: 4; style.border-radius: 8}
}

operator: Plant operator {class: person}
engineer: Reliability engineer {class: person}
equipment: "Plant equipment\n[PLCs, sensors, drives]" {class: external}

platform: "Industrial telemetry platform\n[Software system]\nCollects, stores and analyses\nmachine telemetry; raises alarms" {class: system}

erp: "Maintenance system (CMMS)\n[External]" {class: external}
notify: "Notification service\n[External: e-mail, SMS, push]" {class: external}

equipment -> platform: Telemetry via edge gateways (OPC UA / Modbus → MQTT)
operator -> platform: Watches live state, acknowledges alarms
engineer -> platform: Analyses trends, tunes alarm rules
platform -> notify: Alarm notifications
platform -> erp: Creates work orders from alarms (REST)
